#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generate TFIM graph {#generate-tfim-graph}"
msgstr "Generate TFIM graph {#generate-tfim-graph}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We begin by defining the lattice of spins and the couplings between them. In"
" this tutorial, the lattice is constructed from connected triangles arranged"
" in a linear chain. Each triangle consists of three nodes connected in a "
"closed loop, and the chain is formed by linking one node of each triangle to"
" the previous triangle.\n"
msgstr ""
"Magsisimula tayo sa pamamagitan ng pagtukoy sa lattice ng spins at ng mga "
"couplings sa pagitan nila. Sa tutorial na ito, ang lattice ay itinayo mula "
"sa mga nakakonektang triangles na nakaayos sa isang linear chain. Ang bawat "
"triangle ay binubuo ng tatlong nodes na nakakonekta sa isang saradong loop, "
"at ang chain ay nabuo sa pamamagitan ng pag-uugnay ng isang node ng bawat "
"triangle sa nakaraang triangle.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The helper function `connected_triangles_adj_matrix` builds the adjacency "
"matrix for this structure. For a chain of $n$ triangles, the resulting graph"
" contains $2n+1$ nodes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang helper function na `connected_triangles_adj_matrix` ay bumubuo ng "
"adjacency matrix para sa istrukturang ito. Para sa isang chain ng $n$ "
"triangles, ang resultang graph ay naglalaman ng $2n+1$ nodes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To visualize the lattice we just defined, we can plot the chain of connected"
" triangles and label each node. The function below builds the graph for a "
"chosen number of triangles and displays it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Upang i-visualize ang lattice na katatapos lang nating tukuyin, maaari "
"nating i-plot ang chain ng mga nakakonektang triangles at lagyan ng label "
"ang bawat node. Ang function sa ibaba ay bumubuo ng graph para sa napiling "
"bilang ng triangles at ipinapakita ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For this tutorial we will use a chain of 20 triangles.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa tutorial na ito ay gagamitin natin ang isang chain ng 20 "
"triangles.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/transverse-field-"
"ising-model/extracted-outputs/861ab6e3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/transverse-field-"
"ising-model/extracted-outputs/861ab6e3-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Coloring graph edges {#coloring-graph-edges}"
msgstr "Coloring graph edges {#coloring-graph-edges}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To implement the spin–spin coupling, it is useful to group edges that do not"
" overlap. This allows us to apply two-qubit gates in parallel. We can do "
"this with a simple edge-coloring procedure [\\[1\\]](#references), which "
"assigns a color to each edge so that edges meeting at the same node are "
"placed in different groups.\n"
msgstr ""
"Upang ipatupad ang spin–spin coupling, kapaki-pakinabang na pagsama-samahin "
"ang mga edges na hindi magkakapatong. Pinapayagan tayo nitong maglapat ng "
"two-qubit gates nang sabay-sabay. Magagawa natin ito gamit ang isang "
"simpleng edge-coloring procedure [\\[1\\]](#references), na nag-aatas ng "
"kulay sa bawat edge upang ang mga edges na nagkikita sa parehong node ay "
"mailagay sa magkaibang mga grupo.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Generate Trotterized circuits on spin graphs {#generate-trotterized-"
"circuits-on-spin-graphs}"
msgstr ""
"Generate Trotterized circuits on spin graphs {#generate-trotterized-"
"circuits-on-spin-graphs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To simulate the dynamics of the TFIM, we construct circuits that approximate"
" the time evolution operator.\n"
msgstr ""
"Upang i-simulate ang dynamics ng TFIM, bubuo tayo ng mga circuits na "
"tumantiya sa time evolution operator.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U(t) = e^{-i H t}, \\quad \\text{where} \\quad H = -J \\sum_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_i Z_j - h \\sum_i X_i .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U(t) = e^{-i H t}, \\quad \\text{where} \\quad H = -J \\sum_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_i Z_j - h \\sum_i X_i .\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We use a second-order Trotter decomposition:\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit natin ang second-order Trotter decomposition:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H \\Delta t} \\approx e^{-i H_X \\Delta t / 2}\\, e^{-i H_Z \\Delta t}\\, e^{-i H_X \\Delta t / 2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H \\Delta t} \\approx e^{-i H_X \\Delta t / 2}\\, e^{-i H_Z \\Delta t}\\, e^{-i H_X \\Delta t / 2},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $H_X = -h \\sum_i X_i$ and $H_Z = -J \\sum_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_i"
" Z_j$.\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $H_X = -h \\sum_i X_i$ at ang $H_Z = -J \\sum_{\\langle i,j "
"\\rangle} Z_i Z_j$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The $H_X$ term is implemented with layers of `RX` rotations.\n"
msgstr "Ang $H_X$ term ay ipinatupad gamit ang mga layer ng `RX` rotations.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The $H_Z$ term is implemented with layers of `RZZ` gates along the edges of "
"the interaction graph.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang $H_Z$ term ay ipinatupad gamit ang mga layer ng `RZZ` gates kasama ng "
"mga edges ng interaction graph.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The angles of these gates are determined by the transverse field $h$, the "
"coupling constant $J$, and the time step $\\Delta t$. By stacking multiple "
"Trotter steps, we generate circuits of increasing depth that approximate the"
" system's dynamics. The functions `generate_tfim_circ_custom_graph` and "
"`trotter_circuits` construct a Trotterized quantum circuit from an arbitrary"
" spin interaction graph.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga angles ng gates na ito ay tinutukoy ng transverse field $h$, ng "
"coupling constant $J$, at ng time step $\\Delta t$. Sa pamamagitan ng pag-"
"stack ng maraming Trotter steps, bumubuo tayo ng mga circuits na may "
"tumataas na depth na tumantiya sa dynamics ng system. Ang mga functions na "
"`generate_tfim_circ_custom_graph` at `trotter_circuits` ay bumubuo ng "
"Trotterized quantum circuit mula sa arbitrary spin interaction graph.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Estimate single-qubit magnetizations $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ {#estimate-"
"single-qubit-magnetizations-langle-z-i-rangle}"
msgstr ""
"Estimate single-qubit magnetizations $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ {#estimate-"
"single-qubit-magnetizations-langle-z-i-rangle}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To study the dynamics of the model, we want to measure the magnetization of "
"each qubit, defined by the expectation value $\\langle Z_i \\rangle = "
"\\langle \\psi | Z_i | \\psi \\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Upang pag-aralan ang dynamics ng model, nais nating sukatin ang "
"magnetization ng bawat qubit, na tinukoy ng expectation value $\\langle Z_i "
"\\rangle = \\langle \\psi | Z_i | \\psi \\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In simulations, we can compute this directly from the measurement outcomes. "
"The function `z_expectation` processes the bitstring counts and returns the "
"value of $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ for a chosen qubit index. On real hardware,"
" we evaluate the same quantity by specifying the Pauli operator using the "
"function `generate_z_observables`, and then the backend computes the "
"expectation value.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mga simulations, maari nating kalkulahin ito nang direkta mula sa "
"measurement outcomes. Ang function na `z_expectation` ay pumoproseso ng "
"bitstring counts at ibinabalik ang value ng $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ para sa "
"napiling qubit index. Sa tunay na hardware, sinusuri natin ang parehong "
"quantity sa pamamagitan ng pagtukoy ng Pauli operator gamit ang function na "
"`generate_z_observables`, at pagkatapos ay kinakalkula ng backend ang "
"expectation value.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now define the parameters for generating the Trotterized circuits. In "
"this tutorial, the lattice is a chain of 20 connected triangles, which "
"corresponds to a 41-qubit system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tutukuyin na natin ngayon ang mga parameters para sa pagbuo ng Trotterized "
"circuits. Sa tutorial na ito, ang lattice ay isang chain ng 20 nakakonektang"
" triangles, na tumutugma sa isang 41-qubit system.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-"
"primitives}"
msgstr ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-"
"primitives}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run MPS simulation {#run-mps-simulation}"
msgstr "Run MPS simulation {#run-mps-simulation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The list of Trotterized circuits is executed using the "
"`matrix_product_state` simulator with an arbitrary choice of $4096$ shots. "
"The MPS method provides an efficient approximation of the circuit dynamics, "
"with accuracy determined by the chosen bond dimension. For the system sizes "
"considered here, the default bond dimension is sufficient to capture the "
"magnetization dynamics with high fidelity. The raw counts are normalized, "
"and from these we compute the single-qubit expectation values $\\langle Z_i "
"\\rangle$ at each Trotter step. Finally, we calculate the average over all "
"qubits to obtain a single curve that shows how the magnetization changes "
"over time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang listahan ng Trotterized circuits ay isinagawa gamit ang "
"`matrix_product_state` simulator na may arbitrary na pagpili ng $4096$ "
"shots. Ang MPS method ay nagbibigay ng efficient approximation ng circuit "
"dynamics, na may accuracy na tinutukoy ng napiling bond dimension. Para sa "
"mga laki ng system na isinasaalang-alang dito, ang default bond dimension ay"
" sapat na upang makuha ang magnetization dynamics na may mataas na fidelity."
" Ang raw counts ay na-normalize, at mula dito ay kinakalkula natin ang "
"single-qubit expectation values $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ sa bawat Trotter "
"step. Sa wakas, kinakalkula natin ang average sa lahat ng qubits upang "
"makakuha ng isang curve na nagpapakita kung paano nagbabago ang "
"magnetization sa paglipas ng panahon.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run on hardware {#run-on-hardware}"
msgstr "Run on hardware {#run-on-hardware}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run on hardware with Fire Opal {#run-on-hardware-with-fire-opal}"
msgstr "Run on hardware with Fire Opal {#run-on-hardware-with-fire-opal}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We evaluate the magnetization dynamics on real quantum hardware. Fire Opal "
"provides a Qiskit Function that extends the standard Qiskit Runtime "
"Estimator primitive with automated error suppression and performance "
"management. We submit the Trotterized circuits directly to an IBM&reg; "
"backend while Fire Opal handles the noise-aware execution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sinusuri natin ang magnetization dynamics sa tunay na quantum hardware. Ang "
"Fire Opal ay nagbibigay ng isang Qiskit Function na pinalalawig ang "
"karaniwang Qiskit Runtime Estimator primitive na may automated error "
"suppression at performance management. Isinusubmit natin ang Trotterized "
"circuits nang direkta sa isang IBM&reg; backend habang hinahawakan ng Fire "
"Opal ang noise-aware execution.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We prepare a list of `pubs`, where each item contains a circuit and the "
"corresponding Pauli-Z observables. These are passed to Fire Opal's estimator"
" function, which returns the expectation values $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ for "
"each qubit at each Trotter step. The results can then be averaged over "
"qubits to obtain the magnetization curve from hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Naghahanda tayo ng isang listahan ng `pubs`, kung saan ang bawat item ay "
"naglalaman ng circuit at ng kaukulang Pauli-Z observables. Ang mga ito ay "
"ipinasa sa estimator function ng Fire Opal, na nagbabalik ng expectation "
"values $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ para sa bawat qubit sa bawat Trotter step. "
"Ang mga resulta ay maaaring i-average sa mga qubits upang makuha ang "
"magnetization curve mula sa hardware.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
